      "title": "Nursing Clinical Instructors, Part-Time",
      "description": "Bellarmine University\nJob Posting: Nursing Clinical Instructors, Part-Time Bellarmine University \n\tJob Posting: Nursing Clinical Instructors, Part-Time Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Nursing Clinical Instructors, Part-Time Category: Adjunct Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Locations: Louisville, KY Posted: Mar 24, 2016 Closes: Aug 31, 2027 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Part-time Temporary Position ID: 69944 Share About Bellarmine University: Bellarmine University is a dynamic, growing university with a strong liberal arts focus in the Catholic higher education tradition and a bold vision for the future. Bellarmine has undergraduate and graduate enrollment of nearly 3,500 students and continues to add new academic programs while maintaining small class sizes and personal attention to students. Bellarmine is listed in The Princeton Review 's Best 385 Colleges, is one of the top 20 Southern regional universities in U.S. News and World Report 's 2019 college rankings and is a top university in Forbes ' list of America's best colleges. In a survey by The Princeton Review , students praised Bellarmine as a place that is \"welcoming to every single person and makes an effort to include everyone.\" Bellarmine students, faculty and staff engage in more than 25,000 cumulative hours of service each year, in Louisville and around the nation and world. Bellarmine is located on a scenic 145-acre campus in the Highlands neighborhood and 46+ acres off-campus in Louisville, KY, which Forbes recently recognized as a \"Top 15 City\" for affordable living and National Geographic calls one of the \"Best Small Cities in the U.S.\" Louisville is within a day's drive of two-thirds of the U.S. population. Bellarmine is an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer and encourages applicants with diverse backgrounds to apply. Bellarmine is committed to core values of diversity, equity, and inclusion. Bellarmine will demonstrate a fully realized and lived commitment to equity and inclusion, empowering all members of its increasingly diverse community and supporting them to achieve their full potential. Job Description: The Lansing School of Nursing at Bellarmine University has an ongoing need for qualified part-time instructors to provide clinical instruction in a variety of clinical nursing courses, including adult medical-surgical, critical care, pediatric, women's health, psychiatric-mental health, and community health nursing. ***Visa Sponsorship not provided for this position. Requirements: Minimum requirements include a Bachelor's degree in nursing; two years of full-time (or the equivalent) clinical practice experience in the clinical specialty area in the last 5 years; and a license to practice as a professional registered nurse in Kentucky or Indiana is required. MSN and prior teaching experience preferred. Additional Information: Bellarmine University is committed to core values of diversity, equity and inclusion and embraces diversity in our workforce among members of faculty, staff and administration. We remain committed to affirmative actions, policies, procedures and attitudes necessary to continue to build and retain a diverse and equitable workforce. We will demonstrate a fully realized and lived commitment to equity and inclusion, empowering all members of our increasingly diverse community and supporting them to achieve their full potential. As part of Bellarmine's commitment to diversity, equity and inclusion, we will seek to ensure that all aspects of employment, including recruitment, selection, job assignment, training, compensation, benefits, discipline, promotion, layoff and termination processes remain free of discrimination based upon race, color, national origin, religion, sex, age, creed, sexual orientation, gender identity/expression, genetic information, disability, veteran status, or any other protected class. Application Instructions: Applications are being accepted on an on-going basis.  Please submit a letter of interest, resume and the names and contact information for three professional references by clicking on the appropriate link contained in this posting. Bellarmine University requires COVID-19 vaccination for all students, faculty and staff. Individuals may request exemption from the vaccine requirement for medical or religious reasons. More information may be found at https://www.bellarmine.edu/welcome-back/ URL: www.bellarmine.edu/lansing/nursing.aspx Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2001 Newburg Rd, Louisville, KY 40205"
    },
    "https://bellarmine.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=202704": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Information Systems and Artificial Intelligence",
      "description": "Bellarmine University\nJob Posting: Assistant or Associate Professor of Information Systems and Artificial Intelligence Bellarmine University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant or Associate Professor of Information Systems and Artificial Intelligence Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant or Associate Professor of Information Systems and Artificial Intelligence Category: Faculty Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: School of Business-Business Locations: Louisville, KY Posted: Jul 16, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Exempt Position ID: 202704 Share About Bellarmine University: Bellarmine University is a dynamic, growing university with a strong liberal arts focus in the Catholic higher education tradition and a bold vision for the future. Bellarmine has undergraduate and graduate enrollment of approximately 3,200 students and continues to add new academic programs while maintaining small class sizes and personal attention to students. Bellarmine is listed in the Princeton Review's Best 387 Colleges and is recognized as a top U.S. university in rankings published by U.S. News & World Report and Forbes. In a survey by The Princeton Review, students praised Bellarmine as a place that is \"welcoming to every single person and makes an effort to include everyone.\" Bellarmine students, faculty and staff engage in more than 25,000 cumulative hours of service each year, in Louisville and around the nation and world. SmartAsset ranked Louisville among the top 25 U.S. cities for best work-life balance, while workplace insights platform kununu.com named Louisville one of the top five U.S. cities for happy employees. Glassdoor recently recognized Louisville as one of the top 15 cities for jobs, based on hiring opportunity, cost of living and job satisfaction. ZipRecruiter calls Louisville a top 10 city for job seekers, thanks in part to its central location and low unemployment. Louisville is within a day's drive of two-thirds of the U.S. population. Deeply embedded in the heart of Louisville, Bellarmine is an engaged partner expanding learning opportunities, enhancing career networks and economic growth, and advancing equity and quality of life for its neighboring communities. By connecting the campus, the community, and the curriculum through engaged scholarship and action, we enhance social and civic engagement, including faculty, staff, and student-led, asset-based initiatives. Bellarmine is an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer and encourages applicants with diverse backgrounds to apply. Job Description: Position Summary The W. Fielding Rubel School of Business is the only private business school in Kentucky accredited by AACSB and was recognized among The Princeton Review's Best Business Schools in the South in 2026. We invite applications for a full-time faculty position in Business Technology and Artificial Intelligence, beginning in Fall 2027. The appointment will be at the assistant or associate professor rank, commensurate with the candidate's teaching experience and professional qualifications. We seek an innovative educator and engaged scholar who can help prepare students and professionals to lead in an increasingly technology-driven business environment. The successful candidate will contribute to undergraduate and graduate programs and support initiatives in artificial intelligence, business technology, digital transformation, and emerging technologies. The ideal candidate will possess expertise in information systems, artificial intelligence, business technology, digital innovation, or a closely related field. Candidates should demonstrate the ability to translate complex technological concepts into practical applications for business leaders and professionals. Bellarmine's W. Fielding Rubel School of Business is committed to academic excellence, integrity, social responsibility, and making an impact on our local community. We promote strong ethical principles, fairness, and respect for the dignity of every individual. In the spirit of Thomas Merton, the School provides a student-centered Catholic liberal arts business education. Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. Primary Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate courses in information systems, business technology, artificial intelligence, and related disciplines. Contribute to curriculum development in areas related to emerging technologies, digital transformation, and business innovation. Engage in scholarly and professional activities consistent with AACSB expectations. Participate in assessment, advising, and university service activities. Support partnerships with industry and community organizations to enhance student learning and workforce development initiatives. Desired Areas of Expertise Preference will be given to candidates with expertise in one or more of the following areas: Artificial Intelligence (including Generative AI and AI Governance & Ethics) Business Information System Business Analytics Data-Driven Decision Making Emerging Technologies and Digital Innovation Requirements: Qualifications Required: Ph.D. in Information Systems, Management Information Systems, Business Analytics, Artificial Intelligence, Computer Science, Technology Management, or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution. Doctoral candidates with an expected completion date of July 2027 are encouraged to apply. ABDs within one year of completion will be considered. An earned doctorate is necessary for rank at the assistant or higher level. Candidates should have a strong commitment to teaching excellence and the mentoring of students. Candidates should have a well-defined research agenda and the potential to publish in quality peer-reviewed journals within their area of expertise. Preferred: Experience teaching graduate students and working professionals. Industry experience involving technology implementation, analytics, digital transformation, or artificial intelligence. Ability to teach in multiple modalities, including online and hybrid formats. Interest in collaborating with external partners on applied projects, workforce development initiatives, and executive education programming. Application Instructions: Interested candidates should submit a letter of application describing their qualifications for the position; a curriculum vitae with contact information for three references; a statement of teaching philosophy; and a statement of research or evidence of a research agenda. Applications will be reviewed as received and will continue until the position is filled. URL: www.bellarmine.edu/rubel-school-of-business/index.php Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2001 Newburg Rd, Louisville, KY 40205"
    },
    "https://bellarmine.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=189745": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing - Nurse Anesthesia (Part-Time)",
      "description": "Bellarmine University\nJob Posting: Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing - Nurse Anesthesia (Part-Time) Bellarmine University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing - Nurse Anesthesia (Part-Time) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing - Nurse Anesthesia (Part-Time) Category: Faculty Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: College of Health Professions-School of Nursing & Clinical Sciences Locations: Louisville, KY Posted: Jun 30, 2025 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-time Exempt Position ID: 189745 Share About Bellarmine University: Bellarmine University is a dynamic, growing university with a strong liberal arts focus in the Catholic higher education tradition and a bold vision for the future. Bellarmine has undergraduate and graduate enrollment of approximately 3,200 students and continues to add new academic programs while maintaining small class sizes and personal attention to students. Bellarmine is listed in the Princeton Review's Best 387 Colleges and is recognized as a top U.S. university in rankings published by U.S. News & World Report and Forbes. In a survey by The Princeton Review, students praised Bellarmine as a place that is \"welcoming to every single person and makes an effort to include everyone.\" Bellarmine students, faculty and staff engage in more than 25,000 cumulative hours of service each year, in Louisville and around the nation and world. SmartAsset ranked Louisville among the top 25 U.S. cities for best work-life balance, while workplace insights platform kununu.com named Louisville one of the top five U.S. cities for happy employees. Glassdoor recently recognized Louisville as one of the top 15 cities for jobs, based on hiring opportunity, cost of living and job satisfaction. ZipRecruiter calls Louisville a top 10 city for job seekers, thanks in part to its central location and low unemployment. Louisville is within a day's drive of two-thirds of the U.S. population. Deeply embedded in the heart of Louisville, Bellarmine is an engaged partner expanding learning opportunities, enhancing career networks and economic growth, and advancing equity and quality of life for its neighboring communities. By connecting the campus, the community, and the curriculum through engaged scholarship and action, we enhance social and civic engagement, including faculty, staff, and student-led, asset-based initiatives. Bellarmine is an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer and encourages applicants with diverse backgrounds to apply. Job Description: The Assistant/Associate Professor of Nursing for the Nurse Anesthesia program is a Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist (CRNA) with preferred doctoral degree who contributes to the academic mission of Bellarmine University through teaching, service, and scholarship. This part-time, 12-month faculty role focuses on delivering high-quality didactic, simulation, and clinical instruction to nurse anesthesia students in the Doctor of Nursing Practice (DNP) program. Faculty in this role collaborate with program leadership and clinical partners to ensure excellence in anesthesia education and compliance with the standards of the Council on Accreditation (COA) of Nurse Anesthesia Educational Programs. The position requires ongoing engagement in professional practice, curriculum development, student evaluation, and the support of a diverse and inclusive learning environment. This is a part-time faculty appointment with rank (Assistant or Associate Professor) commensurate with experience and qualifications. Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. Requirements: Doctoral degree in nursing RN License to practice nursing in Kentucky or ability to obtain such licensing if hired. Certified Registered Nurse Anesthetist Application Instructions: Please submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. Please note: Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2001 Newburg Rd, Louisville, KY 40205"
