    "https://bellarmine.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204767": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Campus Recreation & Wellness",
      "description": "Bellarmine University\nJob Posting: Assistant Director of Campus Recreation & Wellness Bellarmine University \n\tJob Posting: Assistant Director of Campus Recreation & Wellness Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Assistant Director of Campus Recreation & Wellness Category: Staff  Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Student Affairs-Sports, Recreation, & Fitness Locations: Louisville, KY Posted: Sep 14, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Exempt Position ID: 204767 Share About Bellarmine University: Bellarmine University is a dynamic, growing university with a strong liberal arts focus in the Catholic higher education tradition and a bold vision for the future. Bellarmine has undergraduate and graduate enrollment of approximately 3,200 students and continues to add new academic programs while maintaining small class sizes and personal attention to students. Bellarmine is listed in the Princeton Review's Best 387 Colleges and is recognized as a top U.S. university in rankings published by U.S. News & World Report and Forbes. In a survey by The Princeton Review, students praised Bellarmine as a place that is \"welcoming to every single person and makes an effort to include everyone.\" Bellarmine students, faculty and staff engage in more than 25,000 cumulative hours of service each year, in Louisville and around the nation and world. SmartAsset ranked Louisville among the top 25 U.S. cities for best work-life balance, while workplace insights platform kununu.com named Louisville one of the top five U.S. cities for happy employees. Glassdoor recently recognized Louisville as one of the top 15 cities for jobs, based on hiring opportunity, cost of living and job satisfaction. ZipRecruiter calls Louisville a top 10 city for job seekers, thanks in part to its central location and low unemployment. Louisville is within a day's drive of two-thirds of the U.S. population. Deeply embedded in the heart of Louisville, Bellarmine is an engaged partner expanding learning opportunities, enhancing career networks and economic growth, and advancing equity and quality of life for its neighboring communities. By connecting the campus, the community, and the curriculum through engaged scholarship and action, we enhance social and civic engagement, including faculty, staff, and student-led, asset-based initiatives. Bellarmine is an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer and encourages applicants with diverse backgrounds to apply. Job Description: The Assistant Director of Campus Recreation provides leadership and operational oversight for campus recreation programs and facilities, including intramural sports, club sports, outdoor recreation, and facility operations. The position is responsible for program development, student staff supervision, facility scheduling, equipment management, assessment, and participant engagement. Working closely with the Director of Campus Recreation and Wellness, the Assistant Director creates inclusive and engaging recreational experiences that promote student involvement, well-being, leadership development, and community. PRIMARY RESPONSIBILITIES Intramural Sports Lead the planning, implementation, promotion, and assessment of a comprehensive intramural sports program. Recruit, train, supervise, and evaluate student officials and program staff. Develop league structures, tournaments, special events, and participation initiatives that foster student engagement and belonging. Club Sports Provide strategic leadership and administrative oversight for the Club Sports program. Advise club officers and student leaders. Manage club budgets, travel requests, risk management processes, and university policy compliance. Support leadership development and organizational growth for all club sports organizations. Outdoor Recreation Coordinate trip planning, risk management, equipment inventory, and participant education. Facility Operations Support the day-to-day operation of the campus recreation center and associated recreation spaces. Coordinate facility scheduling, reservations, and space utilization for recreation programs, athletics, student organizations, conferences, camps, and university events. Supervise facility student staff including hiring, training, scheduling, and performance management. Oversee equipment maintenance, inventory, vendor coordination, and facility inspections. Ensure facilities operate in accordance with risk management standards and university policies. Requirements: REQUIREMENTS: Bachelor's degree required, master's degree in sports and recreation, higher education and student affairs, exercise science, or related field preferred. At least one year of paraprofessional experience working with college students in campus recreation required, and supervisory experience preferred. Administrative and computer skills, web-based applications, and social media experience are core to this position. Attention to detail, strong organizational and interpersonal communication skills, and ability to multi-task are also valued. Some lifting is needed (weight does not typically exceed 50 pounds). Application Instructions: Please submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. Please note: Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. URL: bellarmine.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2001 Newburg Rd, Louisville, KY 40205"
    },
    "https://bellarmine.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205380": {
      "title": "Associate Director of the Bellarmine Fund",
      "description": "Bellarmine University\nJob Posting: Associate Director of the Bellarmine Fund Bellarmine University \n\tJob Posting: Associate Director of the Bellarmine Fund Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Associate Director of the Bellarmine Fund Category: Staff  Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Development & Alumni Relations-Development Office Locations: Louisville, KY Posted: Sep 30, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Exempt Position ID: 205380 Share About Bellarmine University: Bellarmine University is a dynamic, growing university with a strong liberal arts focus in the Catholic higher education tradition and a bold vision for the future. Bellarmine has undergraduate and graduate enrollment of approximately 3,200 students and continues to add new academic programs while maintaining small class sizes and personal attention to students. Bellarmine is listed in the Princeton Review's Best 387 Colleges and is recognized as a top U.S. university in rankings published by U.S. News & World Report and Forbes. In a survey by The Princeton Review, students praised Bellarmine as a place that is \"welcoming to every single person and makes an effort to include everyone.\" Bellarmine students, faculty and staff engage in more than 25,000 cumulative hours of service each year, in Louisville and around the nation and world. SmartAsset ranked Louisville among the top 25 U.S. cities for best work-life balance, while workplace insights platform kununu.com named Louisville one of the top five U.S. cities for happy employees. Glassdoor recently recognized Louisville as one of the top 15 cities for jobs, based on hiring opportunity, cost of living and job satisfaction. ZipRecruiter calls Louisville a top 10 city for job seekers, thanks in part to its central location and low unemployment. Louisville is within a day's drive of two-thirds of the U.S. population. Deeply embedded in the heart of Louisville, Bellarmine is an engaged partner expanding learning opportunities, enhancing career networks and economic growth, and advancing equity and quality of life for its neighboring communities. By connecting the campus, the community, and the curriculum through engaged scholarship and action, we enhance social and civic engagement, including faculty, staff, and student-led, asset-based initiatives. Job Description: Reporting to the Director of the Bellarmine Fund and President's Society and serving as a key member of the Development and Alumni Relations team, the Associate Director of the Bellarmine Fund plays an important role in developing and executing a comprehensive, multi-channel annual giving and donor engagement program designed to increase participation, strengthen donor retention, grow philanthropic support, and build the pipeline for future major gifts. The Associate Director will help lead annual giving strategies across direct mail, email, digital fundraising, crowdfunding, giving days, peer-to-peer campaigns, social media, and other emerging channels. The position will be particularly responsible for developing innovative digital fundraising strategies, strengthening annual giving donor relations and stewardship, managing key annual giving initiatives, and using data and technology to improve donor acquisition, retention, renewal, and upgrades. The Associate Director will collaborate extensively with Development and Alumni Relations colleagues, campus partners, volunteers, students, and external vendors to create compelling philanthropic experiences that connect donors to Bellarmine University's mission and demonstrate the impact of their support. Responsibilities: Develop and execute comprehensive annual giving strategies across direct mail, email, web, digital, social media, phone, peer-to-peer, and other emerging fundraising channels. Lead major annual giving initiatives including Bellarmine's Annual Day of Giving, Giving Tuesday, Reunion Class Giving, Athletics Month of Giving, crowdfunding campaigns, and other targeted fundraising initiatives. Identify opportunities to expand Bellarmine's use of emerging technologies and digital platforms to acquire new donors, reactivate lapsed donors, engage younger alumni, and strengthen relationships with existing supporters. Partner with Development and Alumni Relations colleagues to create donor recognition, stewardship, and engagement opportunities that strengthen relationships and encourage continued and increased annual giving. Work in collaboration with the Director of the Bellarmine Fund & President's Society on the planning, coordination, and execution of stewardship initiatives for President's Society donors, ensuring meaningful engagement and recognition. Help develop a strong pipeline of annual giving donors who may ultimately transition into development officer gift portfolios and other deeper philanthropic relationships with Bellarmine. Utilize donor data, giving behavior, segmentation, and campaign analytics to develop targeted solicitation and engagement strategies and continually improve fundraising performance. Establish, monitor, and report key annual giving metrics, including donor acquisition, retention, reactivation, participation, average gift, upgrades, digital engagement, campaign conversion, and return on investment. Work closely with Development Operations to develop constituent lists, audience segmentation, campaign reporting, data analysis, and performance dashboards. Collaborate with Marketing and Communications and internal creative partners to develop compelling annual messaging, storytelling, digital content, solicitation materials, and donor communications. Serve as a primary content writer for annual giving solicitations, donor communications, stewardship messages, digital campaigns, and related fundraising materials. Manage and maintain annual giving web content and online giving experiences in partnership with appropriate campus colleagues. Operationalize the annual giving communications and solicitation calendar, coordinating multiple campaigns and ensuring projects are completed accurately and on schedule. Participate in campus events, alumni programs, and other activities supporting annual giving, donor relations, and Development and Alumni Relations priorities. Support and effectively communicate the mission, values, and priorities of Bellarmine University. Contribute actively to a positive, collaborative, innovative, and donor-centered Development and Alumni Relations culture. Perform other duties and special projects as assigned. Requirements: Bachelor's degree required. Knowledge of annual giving and fundraising principles, including donor acquisition, retention, renewal, stewardship, segmentation, and pipeline development. Excellent written and oral communication skills with the ability to develop compelling, donor-centered fundraising and stewardship messages. Strong analytical skills and the ability to use data and fundraising metrics to evaluate performance and inform strategy. Demonstrated creativity, initiative, resourcefulness, and willingness to test new approaches to donor engagement and fundraising. Self-motivated with the ability to think strategically, manage multiple projects simultaneously, and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Exceptional organizational skills, attention to detail, and commitment to quality. Ability to work independently while developing strong, collaborative relationships with colleagues, campus partners, volunteers, donors, and vendors. Proficiency with Microsoft Office and experience with donor databases, CRM systems, email marketing platforms, online giving platforms, or related fundraising technology. Ability to exercise sound judgment and handle confidential donor and institutional information with care and discretion. Ability and willingness to attend campus and donor events and work occasionally in the evenings and weekends as needed. Preferred Qualifications Previous fundraising, annual giving, advancement, marketing, communications, alumni relations, or related experience in higher education or a nonprofit environment preferred. Experience with digital fundraising, crowdfunding, giving days, peer-to-peer fundraising, email marketing, online giving platforms, or related digital engagement strategies preferred. Strong understanding of digital communications and an interest in emerging fundraising technologies, platforms, and trends preferred. Additional Information: Physical and Working Conditions Ability to remain in a stationary position for extended periods while working at a computer. Constantly operates standard office equipment such as a computer, phone, copier, and printer. Must be able to occasionally move through the office to access files, supplies, and meeting areas. Requires ability to lift to 10-20 pounds occasionally (e.g., files, office materials). Ability to communicate effectively in person, by phone, and electronically Regular business hours, with occasional evening or weekend work based on departmental needs. The noise level in the work environment is typically moderate. Application Instructions: Individuals interested in applying for this position will need to submit a letter of interest, resume, and contact information for three professional references. Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2001 Newburg Rd, Louisville, KY 40205"
    },
    "https://bellarmine.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=205356": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor-Loan Coordinator",
      "description": "Bellarmine University\nJob Posting: Financial Aid Counselor-Loan Coordinator Bellarmine University \n\tJob Posting: Financial Aid Counselor-Loan Coordinator Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Financial Aid Counselor-Loan Coordinator Category: Staff  Positions Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Enrollment, Mktg, & Communication-Financial Aid Locations: Louisville, KY Posted: Sep 30, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Full-time Exempt Position ID: 205356 Share About Bellarmine University: Bellarmine University is a dynamic, growing university with a strong liberal arts focus in the Catholic higher education tradition and a bold vision for the future. Bellarmine has undergraduate and graduate enrollment of approximately 3,200 students and continues to add new academic programs while maintaining small class sizes and personal attention to students. Bellarmine is listed in the Princeton Review's Best 387 Colleges and is recognized as a top U.S. university in rankings published by U.S. News & World Report and Forbes. In a survey by The Princeton Review, students praised Bellarmine as a place that is \"welcoming to every single person and makes an effort to include everyone.\" Bellarmine students, faculty and staff engage in more than 25,000 cumulative hours of service each year, in Louisville and around the nation and world. SmartAsset ranked Louisville among the top 25 U.S. cities for best work-life balance, while workplace insights platform kununu.com named Louisville one of the top five U.S. cities for happy employees. Glassdoor recently recognized Louisville as one of the top 15 cities for jobs, based on hiring opportunity, cost of living and job satisfaction. ZipRecruiter calls Louisville a top 10 city for job seekers, thanks in part to its central location and low unemployment. Louisville is within a day's drive of two-thirds of the U.S. population. Deeply embedded in the heart of Louisville, Bellarmine is an engaged partner expanding learning opportunities, enhancing career networks and economic growth, and advancing equity and quality of life for its neighboring communities. By connecting the campus, the community, and the curriculum through engaged scholarship and action, we enhance social and civic engagement, including faculty, staff, and student-led, asset-based initiatives. Bellarmine is an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer and encourages applicants with diverse backgrounds to apply. Job Description: Reporting to the Assistant Director of Financial Aid, the Financial Aid Counselor is responsible for providing comprehensive financial aid counseling and support to prospective and continuing students. Responsibilities include: Provide high-quality customer service to prospective and continuing students regarding financial aid eligibility and processes Analyze federal financial aid applications to determine students' financial need Prepare and award financial aid packages and perform all duties related to the financial aid process Interact professionally with students and parents, including in challenging situations, to resolve financial aid?related issues Utilize and update databases and process applications for financial aid received from students Collect and analyze student financial data to determine aid eligibility and make awards in accordance with federal, donor, and institutional guidelines Evaluate documentation related to unusual or mitigating circumstances submitted by students Exercise professional judgment by adjusting cost of attendance, contribution, or dependency status, as appropriate Assist in the preparation and presentation of information related to federal financial aid, scholarships, employment, and grants, for various campus groups, as well as high school students and parents at meetings, workshops, group discussions, and recruitment events Plan, organize, and administer loan programs, including Federal Direct Loans, Parent PLUS Loans, Graduate PLUS Loans, and alternative loan programs Resolve any issues with direct loans by reviewing the comment codes on the FAFSA form. Process and monitor budgets for institutional loans, create Master Promissory Notes on ECSI (third-party partner) Analyze system-generated reports (e.g., grades, enrollment status, award status) to ensure continued compliance with federal and institutional eligibility requirements Notify students of changes in award eligibility and provide guidance on available options Respond to questions, inquiries, and requests from students, parents, and guardians in person and in writing regarding financial aid programs and eligibility Requirements: Bachelor's degree One year of financial aid experience in a school, college, or university setting Knowledge of financial aid eligibility requirements, application procedures, aid programs, cost of attendance, student indebtedness, responsible money management, and financial planning Application Instructions: Please submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. Please note: Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. URL: www.bellarmine.edu/financial-aid/index.php Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2001 Newburg Rd, Louisville, KY 40205"
