y embedded in the heart of Louisville, Bellarmine is an engaged partner expanding learning opportunities, enhancing career networks and economic growth, and advancing equity and quality of life for its neighboring communities. By connecting the campus, the community, and the curriculum through engaged scholarship and action, we enhance social and civic engagement, including faculty, staff, and student-led, asset-based initiatives. Bellarmine is an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer and encourages applicants with diverse backgrounds to apply. Job Description: Under the general supervision of the Assistant Director of Campus Recreation and Wellness and Women's Club Volleyball, the Club Coach aids in overseeing the Maroon Team and is not limited to the following aspects: preparation of training/practice strategies, pre-game organization, game strategy, mentoring of team, recruiting, and professional communication regarding team matters/individual players. The coach serves in an advisory capacity and recognizes that the club is student-led. Team officers are responsible for club administration, budgeting, travel coordination, scheduling, and organizational decision-making. The coach is expected to adhere to all University, Campus Recreation and Wellness, Club Sports, facility, and risk management policies and to model compliance for club members. The Women's Club Volleyball currently practices on Tuesdays/Thursdays from 8:00 - 10:00 PM in the SuRF Center on Bellarmine's campus. Travel to weekend tournaments (two in fall semester; three in spring semester including National Tournament) is expected. Requirements: Comprehensive knowledge of volleyball. Exemplary ethical conduct, integrity and credibility within sport. Demonstrate a commitment to student/athlete development. Ability to motivate student athletes and to encourage both successful academic development and competitive performance. Excellent time management skills with the ability to manage multiple tasks, to work individually, and to work as a member of a team. Possess a willingness and ability to support a diverse, inclusive, and welcoming environment. CPR/AED & First Aid Certification; Certification must be obtained within three (3) months of employment. The successful candidate for this position will be required to complete a criminal background, education and DMV check satisfactory to Bellarmine University prior to commencing employment. Application Instructions: Please submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. Please note: Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. URL: www.bellarmine.edu/recreation-center/club-sports.php Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2001 Newburg Rd, Louisville, KY 40205"
