Louisville is within a day's drive of two-thirds of the U.S. population. Deeply embedded in the heart of Louisville, Bellarmine is an engaged partner expanding learning opportunities, enhancing career networks and economic growth, and advancing equity and quality of life for its neighboring communities. By connecting the campus, the community, and the curriculum through engaged scholarship and action, we enhance social and civic engagement, including faculty, staff, and student-led, asset-based initiatives. Bellarmine is an affirmative action and equal opportunity employer and encourages applicants with diverse backgrounds to apply. Job Description: This professional position supports the Associate A.D. for Athletics Communication across all facets of athletic communication, including game-day operations, marketing, media relations, social media content, video/broadcast productions, digital and print publications, and photography. Specific responsibilities  include: Manage statistical input at home events. Write previews, recaps, and promotional copy for print and digital media. Maintain social media presences for assigned teams. Coordinate local media and opposing team staff requests for media and credentialing. Serve as the primary media contact for assigned teams, including recruiting appropriate game day staff where applicable, and coordinating directly with coaches and staff. Report statistics to NCAA and conference offices. Work with coaches to nominate and promote student-athletes and athletic personnel for appropriate awards and recognitions. Maintain media archives and statistical records. Oversee the performance of student workers. Design print and digital content including still graphics, media guides, promotional graphics, video, social media, schedule posters, and motion graphics. Design graphics, video, and motion graphics for LED boards at various sites. Coordinate video B-roll capture at various athletic events. Design and maintain athletics YouTube pages and websites. Execute content capturing at Media Days. Photograph athletic events. Coordinate in-game photography, including scheduling and overseeing student photographers. Film video at athletic events. Assist the Associate Athletics Director for Athletics Communication in the day-to-day administrative duties. In-game social media posting for home and away events. Assist the athletics department with operational duties assigned by the Director of Athletics or his/her designee Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. Requirements: Bachelor's Degree required Work experience in marketing, journalism, broadcasting, or athletic administration Proficiency in Adobe Creative Suite, After Effects, graphic design, and photography Ability to visually analyze live athletic competitions. Additional Information: Physical and Working Conditions Physical Requirements Ability to remain in a stationary position for extended periods while working at a computer. Constantly operates standard office equipment such as a computer, phone, copier, and printer. Must be able to occasionally move about the office to access files, supplies, and meeting areas. Requires ability to lift to 10-20 pounds occasionally (e.g., files, office materials). Ability to communicate effectively in person, by phone, and electronically. Working Conditions Regular business hours, with occasional evening or weekend work based on departmental needs. Work is performed primarily in a standard office environment. Variable schedules, including evenings, weekends, and holidays, may be required. The noise level in the work environment is typically moderate. Application Instructions: Please submit a cover letter, resume, and contact information for three professional references. Please note: Visa sponsorship is not provided for this position. URL: BUKnights.com Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation 2001 Newburg Rd, Louisville, KY 40205"
